If `batch_size` is 0, `threads` will be 0, leading to a division by zero when calculating `blocks`. While `batch_size` is typically at least 1 when planning, it is safer to add a guard clause at the beginning of the function.

```
  if (batch_size <= 0) return;
  int threads = min(batch_size, 1024);
  int blocks = (batch_size + threads - 1) / threads;
```

